  "source": "\"The Turtle Dove\", an English folk song; tune and words public domain. Six stanzas as a dialogue: an alto is the one who stays and a bass, an octave under her, the one who goes. The choir comes in once, on the last line. Set 4 semitones lower than the demo, to where every voice here holds its top note.",
